  clock: 5  # 8383
  nonce: '8383'  # 8383
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-16 on dev 81f1a69f88. Limb B is closed by measurement; limb\n(a) is live but MIS-SIZED in this item's own recount.\n\nLIMB B (unmapped top-level paths) -- CLOSED, confirmed live rather than read.\n`smart-test --manifest` after touching each path:\n    .agent/hooks/claude-code/session-start.sh    3 tests   (name-mapped)\n    .githooks/reference-transaction            108 tests   (full root fallback)\n    scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh                 108 tests   (full root fallback)\n    untracked scripts/zz-probe-unmapped.sh     108 tests   (the item's own repro)\nThe 2026-08-01 entry above predicted this from PR #142; it is now measured end\nto end rather than inferred from map_to_tests.\n\nLIMB A (code covered only by map-unreachable root tests) -- LIVE, and the\nnumbers in the recount have moved:\n    root tests            76  ->  108\n    KNOWN_UNREACHABLE     19  ->   25\nThe ratchet held -- every one of the 25 is declared -- but ratchet-exempt still\nmeans per-PR dark, and the set grew by six while the suite grew by 32.\ntest_watcher_lifecycle.py, this item's original 2026-07-29 demonstration, is\nstill among them.\n\nUNFILED WORK THIS ITEM SHOULD PROBABLY CARRY. KNOWN_UNREACHABLE's entry for\ntest_stdlib_version_guarded_imports.py states that closing it means \"a fourth\nderived union in smart-test, beside the docs / catalogue-YAML / playbook ones --\nwhich is filed separately rather than done inside an unrelated catalogue PR\".\nI could not find that item. Searched every tracker title; the tracker has no\nfull-text search, so a differently-titled item could exist. The same comment\nrecords that this gate's defect class cost 2,905 failed tests on the 2026-08-29\npy3.10 nightly, so the residual is not hypothetical."  # 8383
