- op: discuss  # ff48
  at: '2026-09-16T09:00:32Z'  # ff48
  by: agent  # ff48
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ff48
  clock: 7  # ff48
  nonce: ff48  # ff48
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-09-16 by PR #1000 (b10d023b53) + PR #1001 (9c8c8165f0). Limb B\nwas already closed by measurement on 2026-09-16; limb (a) is closed now, and\nKNOWN_UNREACHABLE is the EMPTY SET.\n\nWHAT LANDED. The declarative \"covers:\" marker this item's drain path named, and\nthat the map's own docstring and KNOWN_UNREACHABLE entry after entry asked for\nby name. A root test declares its subjects in its header:\n\n    # covers: .woodpecker/*.yml, scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh\n\nand every changed path matching a glob selects it, BESIDE the name rules. All\n25 exempt tests now declare; every marker was derived by READING the test -- the\npaths it opens, the module it loads by file path -- because a name rule could\nnot reach these and a wrong declaration is worse than none.\n\nMEASURED, in an isolated worktree at the pre-change commit so the probe could\nnot contaminate its own baseline (the first attempt did exactly that -- the old\nscript copied into scripts/ was itself an untracked change feeding selection,\nand every \"before\" came back a uniform 41):\n\n    changed file                              before -> after\n    .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml                  2   -> 115   (no CI gate -> all four)\n    CODEOWNERS                                  0   ->  41   (governance mirror gate)\n    .agent/hooks/_shared/launch-transcript-sync.sh 110 -> 115 (watcher_lifecycle by\n                                                              declaration, not by\n                                                              blunt over-selection)\n    docs/adr/0034-*.md                         15   -> 115\n\nAn ordinary package-source change costs 65 selected test files, so the\ndeclarations do not inflate the common case.\n\nCODEOWNERS AT ZERO IS THE ONE I DID NOT EXPECT. The gate that pins CODEOWNERS\nagainst AGENTS.md's governance surface -- the forge-enforced mirror of the\nno-self-merge list -- ran on NO per-PR change to either file.\n\nA DECLARATION MAY ADD A TEST AND MAY NEVER WITHDRAW OVER-SELECTION, and that\narrived as a failure rather than as a design. smart-test unions the whole root\nsuite for a top-level source the map cannot reach; .githooks/** and\nscripts/lib/** are deliberately un-name-mapped and rely on it. The first marker\nnaming .githooks/* made those paths \"mapped\" and would have traded 108 tests for\none. The existing decision test caught it. The fallback asks --names-only; the\nunion asks both.\n\nTHE HEADER SCAN PARSES NOW, and that defect is worth recording because of HOW it\nreported. _module_header cut at the first line beginning \"import \", which in\ntest_rct_public_api_pinned.py is a line of ENGLISH inside the docstring. The\nmarker sat below the cut, the declaration silently did nothing, and the ratchet\nblamed the TEST as unreachable rather than the parser as wrong -- a failure that\nnames the innocent party. ast knows where a docstring ends; a line-start pattern\ncannot.\n\nCI CONFIG IS NO LONGER DARK. .woodpecker/ and .github/ join the executable\nsurface. \"Editing a workflow does NOT select this test per-PR\" appears verbatim\non four KNOWN_UNREACHABLE entries and closed none of them.\n\nTHE UNFILED WORK THIS ITEM FLAGGED IS RESOLVED. The 2026-09-16 entry noted that\nKNOWN_UNREACHABLE's test_stdlib_version_guarded_imports.py claimed a follow-up\nwas \"filed separately\" and no such item could be found. It no longer needs one:\nthat test declares `packages/*/src/*, scripts/*` and is selected on any\nproduction-source change, which is exactly what the comment asked for.\n\nWHY SATISFIED RATHER THAN NARROWED. The empty list is a claim -- every root test\nis selected by some change that can break it -- and it is worth something only\nbecause the ratchet is two-sided: a test that becomes unreachable fails, and a\nglob matching nothing in the tree has rotted and fails. Both arms verified by\nmutation, as was the header parser (forcing the fallback turns three tests red)."  # ff48
